{"id":"sedar:BRVO-2026-11-05-technical-report-ni-43-101-english-8b11","archive_url":"https://github.com/jaydeepdive/minemodelingpro/releases/download/report-archive/ceo_BRVO-2026-11-05-technical-report-ni-43-101-english-8b11.pdf","report_url":"https://ceo.ca/content/sedar/BRVO-2026-11-05-technical-report-ni-43-101-english-8b11.pdf","company":"BRVO","project":null,"commodity":"Cu","jurisdiction":null,"date":"2026-11-05","title_project":"Luanga","cover_company":"Bravo Mining Corp","extractor":"dt21","extracted":"2026-11-06T14:11:17Z","pages":366,"crs":{"zone":22,"hemi":"S","datum":"SIRGAS","zone_votes":{"22":4},"dem_misfit_m":21.8,"kind":"utm"},"center":[-5.95306,-49.55494],"text_center":null,"block_size":[5.0,5.0,5.0],"density":null,"sensitivity":null,"extent":{"strike":{"n":1,"min":8100.0,"max":8100.0,"median":8100.0,"page":94,"text":"he channel. Trenching across the strike of the deposit has been completed in all three sectors along the full 8.1 km strike length. Results have consistently shown a greater lateral extent t"},"depth":{"n":1,"min":300.0,"max":300.0,"median":300.0,"page":98,"text":"o 150 m of the deposit, while Bravo\u2019s drilling since March 2022 has extended the drill-defined mineralization to approximately 300 m below surface in the Central Sector, to approximately 200 m in the North"},"width":{"n":2,"min":10.0,"max":50.0,"median":50.0,"page":87,"text":"nt mineralized horizon within the Luanga Complex and is hosted in the Transition Zone (TZ). It has an average thickness of 10\u201350 m and is characterized by disseminated sulphides (pyrrhotite,"}},"attitude":{"dip":{"n":1,"median":48.0,"min":48.0,"max":48.0,"page":94,"text":"330\u2014the plate was interpreted as dipping 48\u00b0 towards approximately 270\u00b0, and the hole intersected m"},"dip_direction":{"n":2,"median":135.0,"min":22.0,"max":135.0,"page":38,"text":"ons of the complex exhibit steep dips to the southeast. These sections show that the Ultramafic Zon"}},"geophysics":{"surveys":[{"method":"electromagnetics","page":7,"text":"System HARD Half Average Real Difference HDPE High-Density Polyethylene HeliTEM Helicopter-borne Time-Domain Electromagnetic HPAL High-Pressure Acid Leach HPGR High-Pressure Grinding Rolls IBGE Brazilian Institute of Geography","platform":"airborne"},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":29,"text":"106 Figure 9-7: 2023 HeliTEM survey \u2013 17 first-priority EM targets shown over Luanga geology ..","platform":"airborne","year":2023},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":40,"text":"electromagnetic survey (HeliTEM, 771.2 line-km) and a 50 line-km deep induced polarization (IP) programme initiated in June 2026.","platform":"airborne"},{"method":"magnetics","page":40,"text":"Geophysical coverage includes borehole and fixed-loop electromagnetic surveys, ground magnetometry and micro-gravity over 18.7 km\u00b2, a property-wide helicopter-borne time-domain electromagnetic survey (HeliTEM, 771.2","platform":"airborne","line_km":771.2},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":41,"text":"m at 2.04% Ni and 1.23% Cu in hole DDH22LU047), supported by a deep IP chargeability anomaly, and the Crescent Zone, where 2026 drilling intercepted PGM mineralization comparable to that of the deposit.","year":2026},{"method":"magnetics","page":76,"text":"Four diamond drill holes were drilled, but drilling results were not favourable for chromium mineralization,"},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":95,"text":"Southernrock reprocessed the historical induced polarization (IP) data and SGC reprocessed the historical magnetic data; the reprocessed IP resistivity was inverted in three dimensions and overl","year":2021},{"method":"magnetics","page":95,"text":"Ground Electromagnetics Borehole electromagnetic (BHEM) and surface electromagnetic surveys were conducted by Geomag S.A., totalling 4,265 line-metres.","platform":"borehole"},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":95,"text":"9.4.2 Borehole and Ground Electromagnetics Borehole electromagnetic (BHEM) and surface electromagnetic surveys were conducted by Geomag S.A., totalling 4,265 line-metres.","platform":"borehole"},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":96,"text":"9.4.5 Deep Induced Polarization Survey (2026) A ground IP programme of approximately 50 line-km was commenced on 16 June 2026 across the prioritised copper-gold and","platform":"ground","year":2026,"line_km":50.0},{"method":"magnetics","page":96,"text":"9.4.4 Airborne Time-Domain Electromagnetic and Magnetic Survey (HeliTEM) A HeliTEM was flown by Xcalibur Multiphysics","platform":"airborne"},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":105,"text":"In August 2026 a Deep Induced Polarization traverse across Babylon identified strong chargeability with coincident low resistivity at depth, interpreted by the Company to corre"},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":105,"text":"of a large, high- amplitude magnetic anomaly coincident with a strong electromagnetic conductor and a gravity high defined by the ground micro-gravity survey completed in 2024.","platform":"ground","year":2024},{"method":"gravity","page":105,"text":"The actual diamond drilling programme tested the basal zone of the Luanga MUM Complex.","year":2024},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":107,"text":"Deposits 9.6.3.1 Introduction A property-wide helicopter-borne Time-Domain Electromagnetic (HeliTEM) survey carried out in 2023, targeting magmatic massive-sulphide mineralization, generated 17 priority- one and 16 priority-two e","platform":"airborne","year":2026},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":109,"text":"Additional targets were selected from the HeliTEM survey, combined with regional structures, aeromagnetic anomalies and Cu-in-soil anomalies (Figure 9-8).","platform":"airborne","year":2025},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":110,"text":"A 50 line-km of deep-Induced Polarization (Deep-IP) surveying is ongoing across multiple targets.","line_km":50.0},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":112,"text":"To date, Bravo has drilled 28 drill holes at T5, totalling 5,926.25 metres."},{"method":"radiometrics","page":115,"text":"The host rock is a tonalitic intrusion with a Th+U radiometric signature on the airborne survey. The hydrothermal assemblage, together with the structural control, suggest that the T5 Cu-Au mineralization","platform":"airborne"},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":119,"text":"of massive sulphides, the occurrence of strong and coincident magnetic, electromagnetic and gravity anomalies, further work is warranted at the T6 target.","platform":"airborne","year":2024},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":346,"text":"mapping and soil and rock-chip sampling, approximately 50 line-km of deep IP surveying designed to investigate depths beyond 300 m, fixed-loop and borehole TEM and structural work at T5 and T16 to trace the high- grade shoots al","platform":"borehole","year":2026,"line_km":50.0},{"method":"magnetics","page":360,"text":"2023. Time Domain Electromagnetic and Magnetic Survey. Report on Luanga. Zacharias, O. 2007. Estudos de Flota\u00e7\u00e3o com Amostras de PGM Luanga \u2013 Relat\u00f3rio de Progresso 1.","year":2026},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":360,"text":"platinuminvestment.com Xcalibur Multiphysics. 2023. Time Domain Electromagnetic and Magnetic Survey. Report on Luanga. Zacharias, O. 2007. Estudos de Flota\u00e7\u00e3o com Amostras de PGM Luanga \u2013 Relat\u00f3rio de Progresso 1.","year":2026}],"targets":[{"page":96,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"The preliminary interpretation of that line shows strong chargeability with coincident low resistivity at depth, interpreted as corresponding to the Babylon sulphide mineralization and indicating that it may extend deeper, and at a steeper angle, than the dril"},{"page":105,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"It was generated to test the nickel-copper potential of a large, high- amplitude magnetic anomaly coincident with a strong electromagnetic conductor and a gravity high defined by the ground micro-gravity survey completed in 2024."},{"page":118,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"This anomaly also coincides with discrete magnetic and gravimetric anomalies. Four drill holes were drilled at the T6 target to date. The mineralization apparently responsible for the strong T6 conductor was intercepted in drill hole DDH2406T002 and consists o"},{"page":119,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"The target is part of the current deep-IP survey and additional mapping and geochemical sampling are planned."},{"page":345,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"A deep IP traverse completed in August 2026 identified strong chargeability with coincident low resistivity at depth, interpreted as the Babylon sulphide extending deeper, and more steeply, than drilled to date."},{"page":346,"explained":false,"untested":true,"text":"HeliTEM conductors T39 to T45; drill targets being generated Jupiter, Scorpion, Lynx, Perseus, Musca Cu-Au IOCG/ISCG Magnetic and EM targets on regional structures; Jupiter historical hole 21 m at 0.31% Cu; work to be started Note: intervals are downhole lengt"}]},"rock":{"density":{"n":1,"min":2.99,"max":2.99,"median":2.99,"page":284,"text":"Mt Slurry flow rate 2,624 t/h (50% solids), equivalent to 1,751 m\u00b3/h Solids specific gravity 2.99 t/m\u00b3 Void ratio (assumed) 1.0 Estimated settled tailings volume \u2248 7.07 Mm\u00b3/year Source: ALB, 2026."}},"model_params":{"block":[5.0,5.0,5.0],"composite_m":1.0,"default_cutoff":0.87,"method":"idw","power":2.0,"metallurgy":{"routes":["flotation","roast","cil_cip","ultrafine"],"traits":["refractory","oxide","transitional","sulphide","arsenic"],"recoveries":{"Au":48.0,"Ni":50.0,"Cu":89.0},"summary":"refractory, oxide ore present, transitional ore present, sulphide ore, arsenic-bearing; processed by flotation to concentrate, then roasting, then cyanide leach (CIL/CIP), then ultrafine grinding; stated recovery Cu 89%, Ni 50%, Au 48%"},"deposit_style":"bulk","density":2.99,"dip":48.0,"dip_direction":135.0},"effective_date":"2026-09-